1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,800
Rubicon Cloud: the air response to the CFB Wainwright fire
Oct. 17, 2026 · public flight data · Prime Rogue Inc.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,900
Chapter 1: The fire turns
3:10 to 4:05 p.m. · slowed down

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,200
3:10 p.m.: GOES-18 satellite sees the fire: 76 MW of fire power

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,500
A cold front sweeps in from the northwest at about 77 km/h

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
3:16 p.m.: Front passes the Field 21 weather station (CZWN): gust 82 km/h

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
3:20 p.m.: The satellite sees the fire's heat from 3:20 to 3:50 p.m.

7
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:29,850
3:28 p.m.: Cold front reaches the fire (working model v5)

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,600
3:30 p.m.: GOES-18 fire power jumps to 1,215 MW

9
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:38,500
Orange area: fire spread, working model v5 estimate (weighted median)

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:48,500
3:39 p.m.: Range 2 / Range 15 (model median 3:39 / 3:42); working-model estimates, 10–90%: 3:34–3:58

11
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:50,250
3:40 p.m.: GOES-18 fire power: 336 MW

12
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:58,333
Dashed line: final burn outline, measured from Oct. 20 imagery

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,667
DND: incident “just before 4:00” (Oct. 22 briefing)

14
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:04,667
Four soldiers died. DND said 39 were injured (as of Oct. 22).

15
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:07,567
Chapter 2: The quiet
3:34 to 5:20 p.m. · sped up

16
00:01:07,742 --> 00:01:12,742
3:34–5:20 p.m.: No aircraft at or below 12,000 ft heard within 80 km of the fire

17
00:01:11,417 --> 00:01:15,917
Only airliners passed overhead, at 17,900 ft and higher

18
00:01:13,417 --> 00:01:18,917
Military aircraft usually don't broadcast; the RCAF helicopters DND mentioned are not visible

19
00:01:19,117 --> 00:01:21,817
Chapter 3: The response
4:50 to 6:30 p.m.

20
00:01:24,517 --> 00:01:29,517
~4:55 p.m.: King Air C-FSUG climbs out of the Lac La Biche area toward Wainwright (time estimated)

21
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:36,292
4:58 p.m.: STARS helicopter C-FLCI (STAR03) lifts off at Edmonton International

22
00:01:36,917 --> 00:01:41,917
~40 min: Flight time Edmonton to Wainwright: about 40 minutes

23
00:01:44,917 --> 00:01:49,917
5:20 p.m.: First aircraft heard within 80 km. The quiet lasted 106 minutes

24
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:56,667
~5:35 p.m.: C-FSUG and STAR03 reach the Wainwright area (landings estimated, ~5:35–5:37)

25
00:01:56,667 --> 00:02:01,667
5:34 p.m.: SLG2 takes off from Saskatoon toward Wainwright

26
00:01:59,517 --> 00:02:04,517
5:36 p.m.: CWA921 takes off from Edmonton International toward Wainwright

27
00:02:08,417 --> 00:02:13,417
~5:57 p.m.: C-GWRS climbs out of the Fort McMurray area toward Wainwright (estimated)

28
00:02:15,117 --> 00:02:17,817
Chapter 4: The shuttle
6:30 p.m. to 4 a.m. · sped up

29
00:02:17,937 --> 00:02:24,937
“They were cared for first in Wainwright, then flown to hospital across Alberta by STARS, Alberta Health Services paramedics, and Royal Canadian Air Force helicopters.”

30
00:02:21,677 --> 00:02:26,677
~7:08 p.m.: First departure from Wainwright: SLG2 toward Saskatoon (lands 7:41 p.m.)

31
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:42,667
~9:38 p.m.: STAR03 and STAR11 leave; both tracks end at the University of Alberta Hospital site, Edmonton

32
00:02:50,917 --> 00:02:55,917
Fixed-wing shuttles continue to Edmonton, Calgary and Saskatoon

33
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:16,817
3:31 a.m.: STAR01's track ends at the Foothills Medical Centre site, Calgary

34
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:17,917
~3:53 a.m.: Last departure in the data: SLG3 toward Saskatoon

35
00:03:18,117 --> 00:03:25,817
What this data can't show: receivers hear nothing below about 4,250 ft; military aircraft don't broadcast; landing times are estimates; operators are inferred from call signs.

36
00:03:26,117 --> 00:03:33,817
